1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,533
[Leo] Okay, the big question.

2
00:00:02,553 --> 00:00:04,302
[Leo] Who actually clicks approve?

3
00:00:04,322 --> 00:00:05,884
[Ava] The approval chain decides.

4
00:00:05,904 --> 00:00:09,144
[Ava] It's the route an item takes, one sign-off at a time.

5
00:00:09,794 --> 00:00:13,288
[Ava] There are five default chains: global policy, process,

6
00:00:13,308 --> 00:00:17,693
[Ava] legal obligation, public company controls and project documents.

7
00:00:17,713 --> 00:00:20,313
[Leo] Wait, can I create my own approval chain?

8
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:20,941
[Ava] Yes.

9
00:00:20,961 --> 00:00:24,789
[Ava] Editors can change any default chain or build a brand new one.

10
00:00:25,439 --> 00:00:29,964
[Ava] Open Approvals, edit a chain or click New chain, and name each step clearly.

11
00:00:29,984 --> 00:00:31,477
[Leo] Then who signs each step?

12
00:00:31,497 --> 00:00:32,906
[Leo] Can I just put Chip?

13
00:00:32,926 --> 00:00:34,169
[Ava] Chip has no hands.

14
00:00:34,189 --> 00:00:37,603
[Ava] Assign named people, then choose whether any or all must sign.

15
00:00:37,623 --> 00:00:41,923
[Leo] So if my approver's on vacation, I add a backup and set it to any?

16
00:00:41,943 --> 00:00:42,766
[Ava] Exactly.

17
00:00:42,786 --> 00:00:45,993
[Ava] Mark steps optional too, like works council consultation,

18
00:00:46,013 --> 00:00:48,797
[Ava] and skip them with a note where not needed.

19
00:00:50,047 --> 00:00:51,903
[Ava] The owner clicks Submit for approval.

20
00:00:51,923 --> 00:00:54,836
[Ava] Each approver, in turn, sees it under Waiting on you.

21
00:00:54,856 --> 00:00:57,598
[Leo] So this is where someone actually clicks approve.

22
00:00:57,618 --> 00:00:58,338
[Ava] Right here.

23
00:00:58,358 --> 00:01:02,056
[Ava] Approve, or send it back with a reason the owner can act on.

24
00:01:03,306 --> 00:01:04,993
[Leo] And if Legal sends it back?

25
00:01:05,013 --> 00:01:09,802
[Ava] The owner fixes it and resubmits, and the chain carries on to final approval.

26
00:01:12,852 --> 00:01:15,876
[Ava] Every approval, send-back and reason is time-stamped.

27
00:01:15,896 --> 00:01:17,780
[Ava] That audit trail is your evidence.

28
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:21,697
[Leo] So when auditors ask who approved it, nobody digs through email.

29
00:01:21,717 --> 00:01:22,966
[Leo] Chip's thrilled.

30
00:01:23,616 --> 00:01:26,758
[Ava] Put named approvers on every chain by October 30,

31
00:01:26,778 --> 00:01:29,515
[Ava] and run one test submission end to end.

32
00:01:29,535 --> 00:01:32,778
[Leo] Next time, a policy goes live in 13 countries.

33
00:01:32,798 --> 00:01:34,284
[Leo] Bring snacks.
